Vikram and Betal: The Helpful Neighbor (Raw Story)

id: WBX_100130

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there were two neighbors,” said Betal. “One was kind and always helped others, while the other cared only about himself.”

One day, a heavy storm hit their village.

The selfish neighbor stayed inside his house and did nothing.

But the kind neighbor went out to help people.

He fixed broken roofs and shared food with those in need.

After the storm, the villagers thanked the kind neighbor.

Even the selfish neighbor realized his mistake.

He said, “I should have helped others too.”

Betal then asked, “Vikram, who was truly happy?”

Vikram replied, “The kind neighbor was truly happy because he helped others.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Helping others brings true happiness.
